-- title:
--   Igusa branch through an end of the blown-up supersingular chart
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $q \ge 5$, $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and assume (`hι`) that there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota \xi = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ which (`hK`) equals [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell)^2 M'$, where $H =$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/(q\ell)^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$; thus $K$ is the field generated over $L$ by the image of that function field under the coefficient embedding $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\mathbb{Q}) \to \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ the fraction field of $A$, such that $q \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`); $K$ is an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81), the image of the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\prod$-normalised series `jq` of the modular $j$-invariant. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the chart algebra, i.e. the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A K j` $= j$.
--
--   The data and hypotheses are then, in order:
--
--   (1) A maximal ideal $y \subseteq C$ (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) which is supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$.
--
--   (2) The hypothesis `hArig`, the rigidity input at all supersingular points, summarised here: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak{X} =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` along the middle chart) at which the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ whose associated ideal is supersingular in the above sense, there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism
--   $$e : \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{q+1}))\,v - f\,u\bigr) = S$$
--   of the adic completion of the stalk, subject to: compatibility of $e$ with constants from $A$ via $\sigma$; stability of $C$ under every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ that is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ (in the sense of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) for the data $L, q\ell, \xi, q\ell, (q\ell)^2M', H$) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; the congruence $\tau(a) \equiv a \bmod y'$ for such $\tau$ attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$; for each such $\tau$ fixing $y'$ pointwise modulo $y'$, an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ transporting the action of $\tau$ through $e$, fixing constants, acting on $X_0, X_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$ by a matrix $M \equiv c\,\gamma$ over the residue field with $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$, with $c \equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$ and $c \not\equiv 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; separation of prime ideals of $S$ with distinct tangent directions $(a_1:b_1)$, $(a_2:b_2)$ modulo $q$ upon pulling back to the stalk; a coefficientwise criterion, for primes $P$ of $S$ containing $\sigma\varpi$ with tangent direction $(1:0)$, describing membership of germs of elements of $C$ in the contraction of $P$ by the condition that all Laurent coefficients lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$; and the Hasse-type rider asserting that [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to some $a_0 \in A$, and that its germ corresponds under $e$ to a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ for some $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ leading form takes unit values at all pairs $(a,b) \in W^2$ not both in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   (3) A specified point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$ with germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ (`hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with image $z$ (`hy'`), supersingular in the above sense (`hss'`), and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (`hy'y`).
--
--   (4) One fixed Drinfeld chart witness at $z$: a complete discrete valuation ring $W_1$, a homomorphism $\sigma_1 : A \to W_1$ with $\mathfrak{m}_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, power series $f_1, u_1, v_1$ with $u_1, v_1$ units and $f_1 \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1 \bmod (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ of the completed stalk with $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{q+1}))v_1 - f_1u_1)$, together with the hypothesis `hW₁` asserting for this witness exactly the list of riders recorded in (2) (constants, chart-stability, congruence modulo $y'$ for $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$, the $\theta$/$c$/$M$ equivariance with the $\Gamma(\ell)$ and $\Gamma(q)$ clauses, tangent-direction separation, the coefficientwise membership criterion, and the Hasse rider for `jqNModC`).
--
--   (5) An ideal $J \subseteq C$ which (`hJ`) is the infimum of the ideals $\tau^{-1}$ of the contraction, along $e_1 \circ$ (completion) $\circ$ (germ at $z$), of the ideal $(\sigma_1\varpi_t, X_0, X_1)$ of $S$, the infimum being taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ of $K$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$.
--
--   (6) The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ which (`hB`) is generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, i.e. $B = C[J/\varpi_t]$, and a valuation subring $W \subseteq K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), subject to:
--
--   • `hR1`: $C \subseteq B$, and $K$ is the fraction field of $B$ (every $f \in K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$, $h \ne 0$);
--    • `hR2`: $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--    • `hR3`: $W \cap L = A$; $\mathfrak{m}_W$ is generated by $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_W$ to $C$; and $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W \cap B$;
--    • `hEQ`: the equivariance block, namely (i) for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the Drinfeld relation) with kernel the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with reduction $A \to k$, and such that every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $W$ acts through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) for some $c \in \mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (ii) $B$ is stable under all such $\tau$; (iii) every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is, for some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and associated $\tau$, the image of the contraction of $\mathfrak{m}_W$; (iv) an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ after every such translation is divisible by $\varpi$; (v) any such $\tau$ preserving $y$ preserves $W$.
--
--   (7) The membership `hjK` of [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) in $K$ and `hjC` of the resulting element in $C$.
--
--   (8) A natural number $m \ge 1$ with $\varpi^m = \varpi_t w$ for a unit $w$ (`hmt`).
--
--   (9) A finite set `ends` of subrings of $K$ characterised (`hends`) as follows: a subring $O$ lies in `ends` precisely when there is a nonzero $a \in J$ such that, setting $B_a = C[\{x \in K : x a \in J\}]$, there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$, with every element of $y$ a non-unit in $O$, and with $B \not\subseteq O$.
--
--   (10) A member $O \in$ `ends` (`hOmem`) contained in $W$ (`hOW`), local (`hOloc`), Noetherian (`hOnoe`), containing $C$ (`hCO`) and containing $\varpi$ (`hϖO`), together with a crossing presentation of its completion: elements $c_x, c_y \in O$, a unit $u \in O^\times$ with $c_xc_y = \varpi^m u$ (`hcxy`), an isomorphism
--   $$\iota : \widehat{O} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\bigl(\widehat{A}, \varpi^m\bigr) = \widehat{A}[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^m),$$
--   units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$ of the target, with $\iota$ carrying constants from $A$ to constants (`hιc`) and $c_x$, $c_y$ to $\gamma_U U$ and $\gamma_V V$ respectively (`hιx`, `hιy`), and with $c_y \in \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcyW`) while $c_x \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ (`hcxW`).
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of a valuation subring $W_x \subseteq K$ with the following eleven properties:
--
--   (a) $O \subseteq W_x$;
--   (b) $C \subseteq W_x$, i.e. every element of the chart algebra lies in $W_x$;
--   (c) $W_x \cap L = A$: for $x \in L$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $W_x$ if and only if $x$ lies in the image of $A$;
--   (d) $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring;
--   (e) $\varpi \in W_x$ and $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ is generated by $\varpi$;
--   (f) there is $t \in W_x$ which is residually transcendental over $A$: for every polynomial $p \in A[T]$, if $p(t)$ (formed via the base change of $p$ to $L$) lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ then all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$;
--   (g) the element [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) of $K$ is itself residually transcendental in the same sense: for every $p \in A[T]$, if $p$ evaluated at it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ then all coefficients of $p$ lie in $\mathfrak{m}_A$;
--   (h) $c_x \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$;
--   (i) $c_y \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$;
--   (j) for $b \in C$, if $b \in \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ then $b \in y$, and conversely there exists $b \in y$ with $b \notin \mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$;
--   (k) $W_x$ separates $O$ from the other ends: for every $O' \in$ `ends` with $O' \ne O$ there is $f \in O'$ with $f \notin W_x$.
--
--   In (h)–(k) the memberships in $\mathfrak{m}_{W_x}$ are phrased in Lean as statements over all proofs that the element in question belongs to $W_x$. Note that the roles of $c_x$ and $c_y$ with respect to $W_x$ are opposite to their roles with respect to $W$: $W$ has $c_y$ in its maximal ideal and $c_x$ outside, while $W_x$ has $c_x$ in its maximal ideal and $c_y$ outside.
--
--   This is the construction, at a supersingular point $y$ of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$, of the Igusa branch (exceptional valuation) passing through a prescribed end $O$ of the blown-up chart: a discrete valuation subring of $K$ that contracts to $y$, is residually transcendental in $j_{q\ell}$, crosses the given end in the direction opposite to the Drinfeld branch $W$, and distinguishes $O$ from every other end. It is assembled from the three cited results on the crossing presentation, on residual transcendence of `jqNModC`, and on separation of ends, and is used by the corresponding translation–separation statement further along the construction of the auxiliary level structure.
